BATTERY SIZING
The ideal battery must be:
  	1. supply a high enough voltage and current to be able to easily power all components on the vehicle
    2. be light so total weight is reduced, allowing for aster braking and more predictable cornering
    3. be thin enough so the car can sit lower to the ground, reducing the CG height and hence improving the turn radius

Hence we decided to use lithium polymer (Lipo) battery packs as they are generally lighter and smaller than lithium ion or double A battery packs of the same capacity and voltage.
Lipo batteries are also widely available, coming in a wide range of voltages, current ratings and capacities, making it easier to find one that is optimal

Characteristics of lipo batteries:
  - A lipo battery has a maximum voltage of 4.2v per cell when fully charged and can be discharged down to a minimum voltage of approximately 3.0v, below which the battery becomes permanently damaged due to electrochemical effects.
